<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72183" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ</span></b> , relat. Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>whither,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ μολὼν δώσεις δίκην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					228
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴκησις οἷ πορεύομαι</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				892
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				8
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἤκουσας οἷ προβαίνει τὸ πρᾶγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					836
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ χρὴ βλέπειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					714b
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ</span> (i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἃ</span>) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὲν ἔδει δαπανώμενον . . , οἷ δ᾽
					οὐδὲν ἔδει ἀναλώσαντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Virt.</u>
					378b
				</span></i>
			 ; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ δή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Prm.</u>
					127c
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷπερ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					404
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				403
			</span></i> : freq. c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ μ᾽ ἀτιμίας
				ἄγεις</span>
			<i>to what a depth</i> of dishonour, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1035
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ προελήλυθ᾽ ἀσελγείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					4.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> with Verbs of
			ending, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ φθίνει τύχα</span>
			<i>where,</i> i. e. <i>how, in what,</i> it ends, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				371
			</span></i> ; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ τελευτᾷ κακίας</span>
			<i>in what</i> state of vice he ends, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				181e
			</span></i>. (Orig. loc. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς.</span>)</div>
